Package: samba-adws
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends},
 python3-samba,
 python3-gssapi,
 samba-common-bin
Recommends: krb5-user
Description: Active Directory Web Services for Samba (TCP 9389)
 The endpoint Windows administration tooling expects on a domain controller.
 With it the ActiveDirectory PowerShell module, the Active Directory
 Administrative Center and the rest of RSAT manage a Samba domain the way
 they manage a Windows one, over the WS-* protocols on tcp/9389.
 .
 A pure-Python implementation with no Microsoft component: .NET Message
 Framing, GSSAPI/SPNEGO through samba.gensec, WCF binary XML, SOAP 1.2 with
 WS-Addressing, and WS-Transfer, WS-Enumeration and the IMDA data model on
 top. Every request runs as the principal that authenticated it.
 .
 The code is installed as a payload under /usr/share/samba-adws rather than
 into the Python path: it is two sibling top-level packages named src and
 classes, and neither name may be claimed in a shared site-packages. The
 samba-adws command runs the service in the foreground, checks the
 installation, or drives the supported Linux client.
 .
 The unit is installed and enabled and started only where a provisioned
 directory already exists. On a controller that has not been provisioned it
 is left disabled: the service needs a directory and a host service
 principal name, and starting it before either exists fails in a way that
 points at Samba rather than at the missing domain.
